cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use open-provenance in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "open-provenance: An Open, Offline, User-Governed System for Verifiable Media Provenance and Durable Recovery"
authors:
  - family-names: Sarkar
    given-names: Abu Sufian
    email: abu@cyberdude.com
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/abuXsarkar/open-provenance"
abstract: >-
  open-provenance is an open-source system, built on the C2PA standard, for verifying
  media provenance offline, with user-governed trust (no central gatekeeper) and a
  conservative, honest verdict model. It includes a CLI and a zero-backend in-browser
  WebAssembly verifier, a signing tool, and a prototype "durable" recovery layer
  (perceptual-fingerprint registry plus robust watermarking) that recovers provenance
  after metadata stripping, with a reproducible evaluation harness.
keywords:
  - content provenance
  - C2PA
  - content credentials
  - media authenticity
  - watermarking
  - perceptual hashing
  - deepfakes
  - AI-generated content
